      "title_at_revision": "Reserve energy absorption drop tests.",
      "text": "(a) If compliance with the reserve energy absorption condition specified in Sec. 25.723(b) is shown by free drop tests, the drop height may not be less than 27 inches.\n[(b) If airplane lift is simulated by air cylinders or by other mechanical means, the weight used for the drop must be equal to W. If the effect of airplane lift is represented in free drop tests by an equivalent reduced mass, the landing gear must be dropped with an effective mass, where the symbols and other details are the same as in Sec. 25.725(b).]",
